add("sleeptrain-1x3att3", None, "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["pick_up_put_down", "gentle_method"], "My 4mo was gently trained via pick up put down when she was about 3mo. She took to it super quickly", "Pediatrician agreed; now falls asleep in 10 minutes without crying, naps still contact or car seat.")
add("sleeptrain-1x3att3", None, "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "fear", ["daycare_naps", "contact_naps"], "I’m looking for tips on how to nap train her ahead of daycare at 5.5mo.", "Naps still contact or car seat.")
add("sleeptrain-1x3gj3r", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["free_advice", "ferber", "wake_windows"], "I read every pinned resource here. Just finding this sub before she was old enough to train gave me so much peace. Baby sleep CAN be logical. I don’t have to stay miserable.", "First-time mum of a 5-month-old; free subreddit guides fixed the schedule before Ferber.")
add("sleeptrain-1x3gj3r", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["ferber", "cosleeping", "feeding_to_sleep"], "Pre training : had a solid age appropriate schedule, exclusively co slept, nursed to sleep & contact napped. Woke every 60-90mins. Stayed latched almost all night.", "Before-and-after on day 7 of Ferber.")
add("sleeptrain-1x3gj3r", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["ferber"], "Now : falls asleep in under 5mins at bedtime with no assistance in her own space, wakes 2x to feed at around a 4/4/3 schedule, no false starts, wakes up happy.", "Day 7 of Ferber; only three check-ins needed all week.")
add("sleeptrain-1x3gj3r", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["ferber", "cry_it_out"], "She has cried LESS with Ferber than when I was assisting to sleep at bedtime.", "Contradicts the fear that training means more crying.")
add("sleeptrain-1x3gj3r", "pghbb0m", "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "belief", ["gentle_method", "ferber"], "My baby cried way more when assisted to sleep so tbh the “gentle” methods are actually LESS gentle ironically.", "Reply to a parent using a different method.")
add("sleeptrain-1x3gj3r", "pgjbn5d", "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "belief", ["free_advice", "sleep_training_values"], "I never would have sleep trained just willy nilly for the same reasons. Knowing I had this community to learn & ask for help is really the only reason I did it.", "On what made her willing to try.")
add("sleeptrain-1x3sqmh", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["ferber", "feeding_to_sleep", "cosleeping"], "my baby was as attached as they come and woke up every 30 minutes to eat (breastfed) and co slept literally we were both sleeping so beyond horrible I truly thought there was zero hope. Today we are on only day 2 of Ferber and I’ve had hours to myself.", "Breastfeeding mother's day-two success post.")
add("sleeptrain-1x3sqmh", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "desire", ["ferber"], "I know when I was considering sleep training I couldn’t find a single person who did what I did and hoped I did find someone with a successful story for hope.", "Why she posted.")
add("sleeptrain-1x3sqmh", "pfe35kb", "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "tried_failed", ["ferber", "gentle_method"], "we were trying for about a month for other sleep training techniques before we tried Ferber!", "Reply to a parent whose baby freaks out at check-ins.")
add("daddit-1x4i0jx", None, "partner", "toddler_12_24_months", "success_story", ["maternal_exhaustion"], "ever since she was born our daughter has been absolute shit at sleeping. Any sort of sleeping related problem you can think of we’ve experienced it.", "Father of an 18-month-old only child, saying it finally turned a corner.")
add("daddit-1x4i0jx", None, "partner", "toddler_12_24_months", "advice_given", ["maternal_exhaustion"], "Whatever you’re going through with your kid right now, fight like hell, because they need you and it does get better.", "Closing line of the father's post.")
add("sleeptrain-1x5k2qu", None, "parent_unspecified", "toddler_12_24_months", "success_story", ["cry_it_out", "consistency_failure"], "She was a horrible sleeper, and our only option essentially was extinction method, and we had to do it multiple times. She’d cry for \\~1 hr for about a weeks", "19-month-old now sleeps through with rare rough nights.")
add("sleeptrain-1x5k2qu", None, "parent_unspecified", "toddler_12_24_months", "fear", ["cry_it_out", "guilt"], "Last night, she woke up around 1 AM, and just cried on and off for 1.5 hours? Am I horrible for letting it go for that long?", "Rare night waking after extinction training.")
add("sleeptrain-1x5k2qu", "pgn322z", "parent_unspecified", "toddler_12_24_months", "pain", ["sleep_props"], "I think I’m traumatized from the months I tried going in and then was stuck holding my daughter to sleep because she would cry nonstop any time I tried to put her back down?", "Why she hesitates to go in.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7z0r7", None, "new_mother", "baby_9_12_months", "success_story", ["partner_split_nights", "bedsharing", "feeding_to_sleep"], "So night one my husband had to take over because I am just not able to listen to my baby cry without picking him up.", "Bedsharing since 3-4 months, bottle to sleep, up 6-8 times; parents quit the bottle cold turkey.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7z0r7", None, "new_mother", "baby_9_12_months", "pain", ["partner_split_nights", "maternal_exhaustion"], "He wasn’t sleeping well my husband had to start sleeping in another room.", "Before training.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7z0r7", None, "new_mother", "baby_9_12_months", "fear", ["sleep_training_values", "guilt"], "I was so torn up about it literally feeling like we had to put him in the crib and abandon him.", "Doubts before starting.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7z0r7", None, "new_mother", "baby_9_12_months", "success_story", ["gentle_method", "pick_up_put_down"], "Day 3: he went down for his nap in under 10 mins!!!!! No rocking, In his crib with butt pats. And bed time took under 7 minutes.", "Repeated lay-downs and patting, father on night one.")
add("sleeptrain-1x7z0r7", None, "new_mother", "baby_9_12_months", "regret", ["sleep_training_values"], "After months of torture and stress and exhaustion I am astonished. I truly regret not doing this sooner.", "Three days in.")
add("sleeptrain-1x8hv51", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["ferber", "contact_naps", "feeding_to_sleep"], "I had tried EVERYTHING to get him to sleep. Even the big bed trump card wasn’t working anymore. The last few nights we’ve tried Ferber and it’s working?!", "5.5-month-old contact napper fed to sleep.")
add("sleeptrain-1x8hv51", "phk0u9g", "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "others_said", ["conflicting_advice"], "And Reddit STILL wants to tell me I’m doing something wrong 😭", "After listing how well the baby now sleeps.")
add("sleeptrain-1x8hv51", "phicl42", "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["contact_naps", "ferber"], "Honestly mine only contact napped and I was shocked at how well it worked.", "Reply to a hesitant parent.")
add("sleeptrain-1x9g9fd", None, "new_mother", "regression_4_months", "belief", ["sleep_training_values"], "I was sold on the idea that sleep training caused attachment issues. Then, the 3.5 month sleep regression hit and I faced major sleep deprivation.", "Post title: Day 5 Ferber success from skeptical mom.")
add("sleeptrain-1x9g9fd", None, "new_mother", "regression_4_months", "tried_failed", ["sleep_props", "pacifier", "cosleeping"], "Background: we used to pulled out ALL the stops to get her to bed. Paci, rocking until our backs hurt, dark room, white noise, contact naps, cosleeping at night and feeding to sleep when she woke up.", "Before a pick-up-put-down transition week, then Ferber.")
add("sleeptrain-1x9g9fd", None, "new_mother", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["ferber"], "Day 3: MASSIVE IMPROVEMENT HOLY SHIT I  \n FINALLY GOT SLEEP.", "4-month-old on day 3 of Ferber.")
add("sleeptrain-1x9g9fd", None, "new_mother", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["ferber", "night_wakings"], "From waking up every hour or so, trust me, getting 3-4 hours straight is a massive improvement.", "Modest expectations stated.")
add("sleeptrain-1x9g9fd", None, "new_mother", "regression_4_months", "belief", ["information_overload", "conflicting_advice"], "I wanted to take the time to write this because I feel like there is a lot of BS on social media or the several podcasts I listened to.", "Why she wrote a realistic account.")
add("sleeptrain-1xadgsv", None, "new_mother", "regression_4_months", "pain", ["regression_4_month", "partner_split_nights"], "Baby was waking every 45-90 minutes and needed to be rocked back to sleep only to wake again most of the times we transferred her to her bed. My husband and I took shifts throughout the night for several days and were absolutely exhausted.", "20-week-old in the 4-month regression.")
add("sleeptrain-1xadgsv", None, "new_mother", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["book_purchase", "gentle_method", "room_sharing"], "We followed Precious Little Sleep’s Fuss it Out method where you basically allow baby to cry for a set amount of time (we did 20 mins)", "Book method while still room sharing.")
add("sleeptrain-1xadgsv", None, "new_mother", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["gentle_method"], "Night 3: Put her down at 7:20. She did not cry AT ALL. Fell asleep within 4 minutes. I am in absolute shock. Still am.", "After a full 20 minutes of crying on night two.")
add("sleeptrain-1xadgsv", "phw7m29", "new_mother", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["night_wakings"], "I woke up so disoriented from being able to sleep such a long stretch. Haven’t been able to get that much sleep since like my first trimester haha.", "Night 3 slept 7:30 to 4am.")
add("sleeptrain-1xbuwdk", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "fear", ["ferber", "gentle_method"], "when I tried some gentle rocking in crib/pick up put down, he screamed at me for 2.5 hours even when I had him in my arms. I was so scared for how it would all go down and we were ready to throw in the towel before we even started.", "Doubts before Ferber at 6.75 months.")
add("sleeptrain-1xbuwdk", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["ferber", "gentle_method"], "He cries less overall at night and is less agitated at wake-ups than when I used to pick him up to soothe. I just needed to get out of his way!", "Night 5: asleep in 2 minutes.")
add("sleeptrain-1xbuwdk", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "belief", ["sleep_training_values", "maternal_exhaustion", "resentment"], "Honestly screw all the assholes who try to convince women they don’t deserve rest.", "Closing line of a success post written for the guilty and the hesitant.")
add("sleeptrain-1xchbcv", None, "new_mother", "regression_4_months", "pain", ["regression_4_month", "partner_split_nights"], "My husband and I would take 4-5 hour shifts of holding him. All of this took place over 8 weeks! We were feeling terrible. Chronic sleep deprivation, losing weight, stress.", "Regression from 3-3.5 months, wakes every 20 minutes at worst.")
add("sleeptrain-1xchbcv", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["cry_it_out", "transition_to_cot"], "We have our room back, don’t have to tip toe around, have our nights back of hanging out together, and are getting alllll the sleep we want.", "CIO at 5 months with a move to the nursery crib.")
add("sleeptrain-1xchbcv", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "belief", ["wake_windows", "personalization"], "I also want to mention that wake windows for successful sleep training are very dependent on your baby even with all the guidelines.", "Trained on shorter wake windows than charts suggest and it still worked.")
add("FirstTimeMom-1xcpe2h", None, "new_mother", "looking_back", "advice_given", ["free_advice", "course_purchase", "wake_windows"], "Taking Cara Babies has so much helpful and free information on these topics! We were just winging it for a long time (about 3 months) before we were finally desperate enough to commit to a nap schedule and bedtime routine.", "First-time mother's tips list; free course content, not the paid course.")
add("FirstTimeMom-1xcpe2h", None, "new_mother", "looking_back", "success_story", ["transition_to_cot"], "We struggled SO MUCH to get our baby to sleep in her bassinet for a month before our friends gave us this pro-tip.", "Switching from bassinet to full crib helped longer sleeps.")
add("FirstTimeMom-1xcpe2h", None, "new_mother", "looking_back", "advice_given", ["free_advice", "information_overload"], "there were so many nights that my husband and I would each scour through Reddit looking for answers, advice, or simply commiseration for our struggles.", "Looking back at the first 2-3 months.")
add("FirstTimeMom-1xcpe2h", None, "new_mother", "looking_back", "purchase", ["swaddle_transition", "sleepwear"], "At first we tried to transition her with just the cocoon swaddle, but her sleep was so disrupted that we eventually caved and ordered the Butterfly Cardi.", "Second sleepwear purchase during the swaddle transition.")
